    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d722">

                <pb facs="0806" n="726" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg726"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Buck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 424.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 672, of the 18th ultimo, in regard to the arbitration of the house-tax
                    question.</p>
                <p>The assurance you report as having received from the minister of foreign affairs
                    that the further collection of this tax will be suspended pending the decision
                    of the arbitral court is an apparently satisfactory result of your suggestions
                    in pursuance of telegraphic instructions of January 18 last, to which you
                    refer.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
